    "text": "A thin spherical shell of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;is cut into two equal halves and then each of its halves is charged to the same uniform surface charge density&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>σ</mi></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math>&nbsp;is the force exerted on each half to keep them at equilibrium, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;proportional to<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0005_a207535449e5.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 137px;\" />"
